                "text": "Analyse the examples and solve the task.\n\n**Rule Explanation:**\n1. A cross-shaped divider of a single color (e.g., color 1 in train 1, color 6 in train 2, color 4 in train 3) divides the grid into four quadrants. The background color of empty cells is 7 (orange).\n2. One of the quadrants contains a pattern/objects, while the other three quadrants are filled with the background color (7).\n3. The pattern is reflected symmetrically across the dividing lines (both horizontally, vertically, and diagonally across both lines) to fill the other quadrants.\n   - Specifically, each quadrant gets the reflection of the non-empty quadrant across the horizontal and/or vertical divider.\n   - For quadrants with dimensions smaller than the original quadrant, the reflection is truncated to fit the available dimensions (or aligned relative to the divider lines: reflections are indexed with distance from the divider line).\n   - Let's verify indexing:\n     - In Train 1: \n       - Divider at row 4, col 4.\n       - Pattern in top-left: rows 0..3, cols 0..3.\n       - Top-right (cols 5..8): horizontal reflection relative to col 4.\n         - col 5 is reflection of col 3 (distance 1 from divider).\n         - col 6 is reflection of col 2.\n         - col 7 is reflection of col 1.\n         - col 8 is reflection of col 0.\n       - Bottom-left (rows 5..8): vertical reflection relative to row 4.\n         - row 5 is reflection of row 3.\n         - row 6 is reflection of row 2, etc.\n     - In Train 2:\n       - Divider at row 5, col 4.\n       - Pattern in top-left: rows 0..4, cols 0..3.\n       - Top-right (cols 5..6): width 2.\n         - col 5 (dist 1) is reflection of col 3 (dist 1).\n         - col 6 (dist 2) is reflection of col 2 (dist 2).\n       - Bottom-left (rows 6..7): height 2.\n         - row 6 (dist 1) is reflection of row 4 (dist 1).\n         - row 7 (dist 2) is reflection of row 3 (dist 2).\n     - In Train 3:\n       - Divider at row 2, col 3.\n       - Pattern in bottom-right: rows 3..7, cols 4..9.\n       - Reflected across col 3 and row 2.\n       - Distances measured from the divider line!\n\nI am ready for the test input.",
